# .mjs files MUST check out with LF on every platform: vitest's transform
# pipeline fails with "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token" when an
# imported .mjs (tests/brand-leak-scan.test.ts -> scripts/brand-leak-scan.mjs)
# is materialised with CRLF, which core.autocrlf=true does on Windows.
# Verified A/B/A on i9 2026-08-25: CRLF fails, LF passes, byte-identical
# otherwise. CI (Linux) always saw LF, so only local Windows runs broke.
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Vitest writes snapshot files with LF whatever the platform, so on a CRLF
# checkout (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) the FIRST test run rewrites every
# line and the file shows as modified with a zero-content diff. Three
# separate agents hit this in fresh worktrees on 2026-08-28 and each had to
# work out it was a line-ending artefact before they could trust their own
# `git status`. Pinning it removes the question.
*.snap text eol=lf
